    {
      "@id": "urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A4d53ee5bb82b4562bf890b41c6bf9c154ada3917edc5705a3a91d12a43964493:13704:14298:sha256-89e453fadae9e7c592fddedd72d774975979f33cb9fac1b24b0b77bcc14b94ee",
      "@type": "rkaf:SourceFragment",
      "oa:hasSource": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:document:4d53ee5bb82b4562bf890b41c6bf9c154ada3917edc5705a3a91d12a43964493",
      "rkaf:fragmentIdentityScheme": "rkaf:carrier-local-fragment",
      "rkaf:sourceArtifactDigest": "sha256:4d53ee5bb82b4562bf890b41c6bf9c154ada3917edc5705a3a91d12a43964493",
      "rkaf:fragmentContentDigest": "sha256:89e453fadae9e7c592fddedd72d774975979f33cb9fac1b24b0b77bcc14b94ee",
      "rkaf:selectorKind": [
        "oa:TextQuoteSelector",
        "oa:TextPositionSelector"
      ],
      "oa:hasSelector": [
        {
          "@type": "oa:TextQuoteSelector",
          "oa:exact": "(i) What is the definition of medical treatment? “Medical treatment” means the management and care of a patient to combat disease or disorder. For the purposes of part 1904, medical treatment does not include:\n\n(A) Visits to a physician or other licensed health care professional solely for observation or counseling;\n\n(B) The conduct of diagnostic procedures, such as x-rays and blood tests, including the administration of prescription medications used solely for diagnostic purposes ( e.g., eye drops to dilate pupils); or\n\n(C) “First aid” as defined in paragraph (b)(5)(ii) of this section."
        },
        {
          "@type": "oa:TextPositionSelector",
          "oa:start": 13704,
          "oa:end": 14298,
          "rkaf:coordinateSystem": "rkaf:unicode-codepoint"
        }
      ]
    },
